  "response": "여기 오기까지 망설이셨을 텐데, 그 말 꺼내주셔서 감사합니다. '이런 걸로 시간을 내도 되는 건가' 하고 스스로에게 물으셨을 때, 사실 그게 얼마나 무거운 건지 느끼고 있어요.\n\n소리를 지른 자신에게 놀라셨다고 하셨죠. '저는 그런 사람이 아닌데'라는 말이, 아마 그때 순간이 얼마나 낯설고 당혹스러웠는지 보여주는 것 같아요.\n\n그리고 '그게 전부는 아닌 것 같기도 하고'라고 덧붙이셨는데, 그 말이 눈에 들어와요. 피곤해서 일 수도 있다는 설명도 분명히 있을 수 있지만, 동시에 그 이상 어딘가에서 무언가가 쌓여 있었을지도 모른다는 감각도 함께 있는 거죠?",
  "reasoning": "The user is presenting a counseling dialogue where a client has just shared something vulnerable - they yelled at their child a few days ago, they're surprised by their own behavior, they feel it might not be the whole story, and they're also tired lately. They also express hesitation about whether their concern is \"worth\" a counseling session.\n\nKey elements to address:\n1. The client's hesitation about whether their issue is \"worth\" bringing to counseling - this needs to be validated without being dismissive\n2. The shock/surprise at their own behavior (yelling at their child) - this carries guilt and a sense of \"that's not me\"\n3. The uncertainty about whether it's just fatigue or something deeper - they're already doing some self-reflection\n4. The overall tone is tentative, self-questioning, a bit apologetic\n\nWhat NOT to do:\n- Don't rush to reassure (\"it's okay, everyone does that\")\n- Don't immediately jump to solutions\n- Don't over-analyze or diagnose\n- Don't ask multiple questions\n- Don't dismiss the tiredness or the deeper concern\n\nWhat TO do:\n- Acknowledge that they brought something that clearly matters to them (countering the \"is this worth it\" hesitation)\n- Validate the experience of being surprised by their own reaction\n- Perhaps gently reflect the tension they're feeling between \"it's just tiredness\" and \"it feels like there's more to it\"\n- Maybe offer a gentle question or reflection that helps them explore further, or simply hold space\n\nI think a good response would:\n1. Gently address the \"is this worth it\" hesitation\n2. Reflect back what I hear - the surprise at their own behavior, the sense that there might be more going on\n3. Perhaps validate that being surprised by oneself can be unsettling\n4. Maybe gently open the door to exploring the \"it's not just tiredness\" part, without pushing\n\nLet me write this naturally in Korean, keeping it conversational and warm but not overly effusive.\n",
